0,Jewish music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewish_music,"May 5, 2026 - Ashkenazic Jews named this official ... printed Hebrew versions of the Bible by a system of cantillation marks (sometimes referred to as neumes). In practice the cantillation often echoes the tones and rhythms of the countries and ages in which Jews lived, notably as regards the modality in which the local music was ...",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
1,Afroasiatic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afroasiatic_languages,"3 weeks ago - The Afroasiatic languages (also known as the Afro-Asiatic, Afrasian, Hamito-Semitic, or Semito-Hamitic languages) are a language family (or phylum) of about 400 languages spoken predominantly in West Asia, North Africa, the Horn of Africa, and parts of the Sahara and Sahel.",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
2,Hebrew - heb (Afro-Asiatic) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/heb/,"October 31, 2025 - Hebrew (heb) is part of the Afro-Asiatic family and Afro-Asiatic, Semitic, Central, South, Canaanite class.",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
3,Cantillation and Torah Reading Hebrew Afro-Asiatic Natural,https://www.iaswww.com/apr/Science/Social_Sciences/Linguistics/Languages/Natural/Afro-Asiatic/Hebrew/Cantillation_and_Torah_Reading/,"Ellie Ackerman's pioneering, trope-teaching website: offers Torah and Haftarah cantillation marks online, with real audio, also downloadable (as zip files; electronic sounding)and musical notation for all ta'amim. Website includes: rare notes; Eicha (Lame · Top: Science: Social Sciences: Linguistics: Languages: Natural: Afro-Asiatic: Hebrew: Cantillation and Torah Reading",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
4,Major branches of Afro-Asiatic languages | Britannica,https://www.britannica.com/summary/Afro-Asiatic-languages,"Afro-Asiatic languages, formerly Hamito-Semitic languages, Family of about 250 languages spoken in North Africa, parts of sub-Saharan African, and the Middle East. It includes such languages as Arabic, Hebrew, Amharic, and Hausa. The total number of speakers is estimated to be more than 250 million.",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
5,Hebrew,https://www.mit.edu/~ejhanna/language/hebrew.html,"Hebrew is a Semitic language, along with Arabic and several languages of the ancient Middle East, such as Assyrian and Aramaic, and also many languages of present-day Ethiopia. The Semitic languages are part of a still larger family of languages known as Afro-Asiatic, which, as the name denotes, are spoken in Africa and Asia (although no further east than the Arabian penninsula).",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
6,Is Hebrew Afro-Asiatic? - Quora,https://www.quora.com/Is-Hebrew-Afro-Asiatic,"Answer (1 of 7): Yes. Jerusalem is on the African continent. Hebrew’s descendants are the Negroes in america today. Make no mistake about it. Labeling and sub-dividing is an age old European tactic which in result, causes more gentiles to be confused. There is NO negroe, no afro, no black. Only...",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
