8,Afroasiatic,http://www.languagesgulper.com/eng/Afroasiatic.html,"Classification and Distribution. Afro-Asiatic is divided into six branches: Semitic, Berber, Egyptian, Cushitic, Chadic and Omotic. Semitic and Berber are quite closely related, and both are more distantly connected to Cushitic.",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
9,All In The Language Family: The Afro-Asiatic Languages,https://www.babbel.com/en/magazine/afro-asiatic-language-family,"June 17, 2020 - The most widely spoken Afro-Asiatic language today is Arabic (a Semitic language), but there are many other significant languages in the family. These include Shilha (a Berber language, spoken in Morocco), Hausa (from the Chadic branch — spoken in Nigeria and Niger) and Somali (a Cushitic language native to several East African countries). There’s also Mao (an Omotic language spoken in Ethiopia), and Hebrew (which also belongs to the Semitic branch).",Hebrew,Afro-Asiatic
